{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774207189,"nonce":"IlUS8H6DoKp6PjKSSQZnyFwCcd0=","message":"Design note: foreground vs background subagents and async result delivery\n\n**Agent tool modes:**\n- Foreground (default): blocking — parent waits for subagent completion\n- Background (run_in_background: true): non-blocking — parent gets immediate ack, continues working, receives task-notification when subagent completes\n\n**MCP tool implications:**\nMCP tool calls are inherently blocking. For foreground subagents, mandible_spawn_agent blocks and returns the final result. For background subagents, it returns immediately with a session ID, and results are delivered asynchronously.\n\n**Async result delivery options (ranked):**\n\n1. **Channel notifications** (best) — push notification into parent session via channel server. Only mechanism that both reliably delivers results AND injects into the model active conversation context without polling. Works for Mandible-spawned sessions and channel-connected (1.5-class) sessions.\n\n2. **SubagentStop hooks** — already implemented in buildHooks(). Fires when subagent completes, notifies Mandible, but cannot inject content into model conversation context. Good for dashboard observability, not for model-facing delivery.\n\n3. **Inbox + next-turn pickup** — result lands in Mandible inbox, parent picks up via mandible_check_inbox on next turn. Reliable but not real-time. Fallback for external (3rd-class) sessions. Same pattern as auth results today.\n\n4. **streamInput() injection** — SDK Query object accepts AsyncIterable\u003cSDKUserMessage\u003e. Could inject synthetic user message (\"Agent X completed: ...\") into running query. Fragile — model may not handle unexpected mid-reasoning injection gracefully.\n\n5. **MCP tool polling** — parent calls mandible_check_agent_status periodically. Wasteful, unreliable, latency-prone. The old approach — avoid.\n\n**Recommendation:** Channel notifications for Mandible-spawned and channel-connected sessions. Inbox fallback for external sessions.","files":null}]}